### Planner Response

I have implemented the "Forgot Password" functionality for all users (Students, Teachers, Admin).

### Changes Made:
1.  **Backend ([backend/server.js](cci:7://file:///c:/Users/Intel%20Computer/Desktop/anti/school-portal/backend/server.js:0:0-0:0), [backend/database.js](cci:7://file:///c:/Users/Intel%20Computer/Desktop/anti/school-portal/backend/database.js:0:0-0:0)):**
    *   Installed `nodemailer` for handling emails.
    *   Updated the database schema to include a `password_resets` table for storing secure reset tokens.
    *   Added two new API endpoints:
        *   `/api/forgot-password`: Generates a secure token and mocks sending an email (logs the link to the console for now).
        *   `/api/reset-password`: Verifies the token and updates the user's password.
2.  **Frontend (`src/pages/`):**
    *   **Updated [Login.jsx](cci:7://file:///c:/Users/Intel%20Computer/Desktop/anti/school-portal/src/pages/Login.jsx:0:0-0:0)**: Added a "Forgot Password?" link next to the password field.
    *   **Created [ForgotPassword.jsx](cci:7://file:///c:/Users/Intel%20Computer/Desktop/anti/school-portal/src/pages/ForgotPassword.jsx:0:0-0:0)**: A page where users enter their email to request a reset link.
    *   **Created [ResetPassword.jsx](cci:7://file:///c:/Users/Intel%20Computer/Desktop/anti/school-portal/src/pages/ResetPassword.jsx:0:0-0:0)**: A page where users create a new password after clicking the email link.
    *   **Updated [App.jsx](cci:7://file:///c:/Users/Intel%20Computer/Desktop/anti/school-portal/src/App.jsx:0:0-0:0)**: Added routing for the new pages.

### How to Test:
1.  **Restart your backend server** so the new database changes and routes take effect.
2.  Go to the Login page.
3.  Click **"Forgot Password?"**.
4.  Enter the email of a user (e.g., `admin@school.com` or `alex.j@school.com`).
5.  **Check your backend terminal/console**. Since we are in development mode, the reset link will be printed there (e.g., `Reset Link: http://localhost:5173/reset-password?token=...`).
6.  Open that link in your browser to set a new password.

**Note:** The system is currently configured to log the reset link to the console. To send real emails, you will need to provide your email service credentials (like Gmail) in [backend/server.js](cci:7://file:///c:/Users/Intel%20Computer/Desktop/anti/school-portal/backend/server.js:0:0-0:0) under the `transporter` configuration.

