### Planner Response

The error `Firebase: Error (auth/configuration-not-found)` means that the **Email/Password authentication method is disabled** in your Firebase project. Even if you have the code set up, Firebase blocks the emails until you explicitly turn this feature on.

### 🛠️ How to Fix It (in Firebase Console):

1.  Go to the **[Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/)** and open your project.
2.  On the left sidebar, click **Build** > **Authentication**.
3.  Click on the **Sign-in method** tab (sometimes labeled "Native providers").
4.  Click on **Email/Password**.
5.  **Toggle the "Enable" switch to ON**. (ignore the "Email link" switch for now).
6.  Click **Save**.

**Once you click Save, try sending the reset link from your app again.** It should work immediately.

