I see the image. You are looking at the **Firestore Database** (data storage).

**⚠️ Important:** Firebase has TWO places where users must exist:
1.  **Firestore Database** (Where you are looking now): Stores profile info like `name`, `subject`, `phone`.
2.  **Authentication** (Where passwords live): Stores the `email` and secure `password` for logging in.

The "Forgot Password" feature ONLY talks to the **Authentication** section. It does **not** look at your Firestore Database.

**Checking:**
If `ahmadaziz7172@gmail.com` is **ONLY** in Firestore (the picture you sent) but **NOT** in the "Authentication" tab, the email will **never send**.

